        <Section title="By model" sub="The Cyrus model the build ran on; “auto” = older builds where the service picked the model.">
          <StatsTable rows={statsBy(lite, (b) => b.model ?? "auto")} label="Model" />
        </Section>
      </div>

      <Section
        title="AI cost vs tokens charged (margin by model)"
        sub={<>Settled token holds in the last 30 days ({n(settled.length)}). Value of tokens = tokens charged × a reference price: the top-up price (${(topupRate).toFixed(4)}/token) and, as the worst case, the cheapest plan price (${planRate.toFixed(4)}/token). Real revenue depends on how each customer got their tokens: game-server and admin grants earn nothing directly. AI cost of all builds in the window: {usd(cost30, 2)}.</>}
      >
