// Cyrus mod health telemetry (wiring phase 2): the INGEST path. POST /api/cyrus/telemetry/v1/ingest, body
// { signals: HealthSignal[] } (at most 500, at most 256 KiB), header `x-cyrus-telemetry-signature: <hex
// HMAC-SHA256(CYRUS_HEALTH_TELEMETRY_SECRET, raw body)>`. Only the platform's own collector holds the secret (it runs
// collectSignals, which is where the owner's opt-in is checked). Fail closed at every step:
//   CYRUS_HEALTH_TELEMETRY=1 and a secret of 24+ chars (else 404) -> signature (401) -> size / JSON / count (400/413)
//   -> EVERY signal valid by the strict schema, or the whole batch is refused (422: nothing stored) -> days only
